Nightforge: translate DXMT's shaders when a game creates them, so that the first round waits less.

Off unless DXMT_PREPARE_SHADERS is set (1 = plain variants, 2 = also pixel shaders with all their
targets 8-bit unorm). Translation only (AIR into DXMT's own shader cache): Metal's compile still
happens at the first draw. Local only: no upload, no shipped shaders, nothing hooks the game.

Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Parts come from Recall's DXMT patches (v1.6.3, patches/
dxmt-v1-private.patch and dxmt-v1-performance.patch, https://github.com/AsherJN/recall,
by Joshua Asher Nelson), which are offered under LGPL-2.1-or-later and apply to
https://github.com/NerRobDog/dxmt at c5dc3a0. Changed for the DXMT v0.80 pin by Nightforge,
November 2026; see docs/ENTWURF-SHADER.md for what was taken and what wasn't.

Taken: task_scheduler's limit and priority and its shutdown fix, a real hash for ShaderVariant,
the scheduler joined before the objects it uses, SetCacheOnly and the variant prediction.
Changed: the sample mask stays in the variant (see canonical()), limits on variants, bytes and
fan-out, cache lock at the compile threads' priority, compute shaders prepared too, level 2.

